.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt REBOOT 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm reboot
.Nd halt, power off, or restart the machine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/reboot.h
.Ft int
.Fn reboot "int command"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn reboot
performs the operation selected by
.Fa command .
The caller must have effective user ID 0.
Privilege is checked before the magic numbers or command.
.Bl -tag -width RB_HALT_SYSTEM
.It Dv RB_AUTOBOOT
Restart the machine.
.It Dv RB_HALT_SYSTEM
Halt the processor, leaving power on.
The console displays
.Ql halt: system halted .
.It Dv RB_POWER_OFF
Power off the machine.
If the platform does not power off, halt instead.
.It Dv RB_DISABLE_CAD
Return success without changing state.
Keyboard reboot is permanently disabled.
.It Dv RB_ENABLE_CAD
Return
.Er EINVAL ;
keyboard reboot is not implemented.
.El
.Pp
Other commands are rejected.
The three stop commands perform the kernel shutdown procedure and do
not return.
A restart that fails to reset the platform also ends in a halt.
.Pp
The i386 system call number is 88, and the x86-64 one 169, where the three
arguments are in RDI, RSI and RDX.
Its arguments are a first magic number in EBX, a second magic number
in ECX, and the command in EDX.
The first magic must be
.Ql 0xfee1dead .
The accepted second values are
.Ql 0x28121969 ,
.Ql 0x05121996 ,
.Ql 0x16041998 ,
and
.Ql 0x20112000 .
Musl supplies the first magic and
.Ql 0x28121969
for the caller.
.Pp
The command values are
.Ql 0x01234567
for restart,
.Ql 0xcdef0123
for halt,
.Ql 0x4321fedc
for power off,
zero for disabling keyboard reboot, and
.Ql 0x89abcdef
for the unsupported enable operation.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv RB_DISABLE_CAD
returns 0.
The halt, power-off, and restart commands do not return.
On failure,
.Fn reboot
returns -1 and sets
.Va errno .
The raw kernel call returns a negative error number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The default suite's
.Pa tests/rebootprobe.c
checks
.Dv RB_DISABLE_CAD
with all four accepted second magic numbers, rejects bad magic numbers
and unsupported commands, and checks that an unprivileged child cannot
power off the machine.
It does not stop the machine.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width EINVAL
.It Er EINVAL
A magic number is wrong or the command is unsupported.
.It Er EPERM
The caller's effective user ID is not 0.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halt 8
